{"id": "EUVD-2026-81117", "enisaUuid": "3e0ac213-0651-3690-bb18-fb3cbf81a308", "description": "A vulnerability in the web-based management interface of Cisco ThousandEyes Virtual Appliance could allow an authenticated, remote attacker to inject arbitrary operating system commands.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to improper validation of user-supplied input to the web-based management interface. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by saving configuration details that contain malicious values. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to execute arbitrary operating system commands with root privileges. To exploit this vulnerability, the attacker must have valid administrative credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:10:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-21T12:50:01", "baseScore": 4.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-teva-os-command-W4GAO6jp"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-20350", "GHSA-gvrw-xc72-49qh"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19e32807-2dc7-39a3-8ddb-3ea06e659394", "product": {"name": "Cisco ThousandEyes Enterprise Agent", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "Agent 4.4.2"}, {"id": "1fdc584c-22d7-332b-afc1-e9d0d72f158e", "product": {"name": "Cisco ThousandEyes Enterprise Agent", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "Agent 5.0"}, {"id": "3971c047-f6dc-3a90-8859-e703e313497c", "product": {"name": "Cisco ThousandEyes Enterprise Agent", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "Agent 4.1"}, {"id": "5fe73159-2584-3bd9-bfd6-aae00527ab54", "product": {"name": "Cisco ThousandEyes Enterprise Agent", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "Agent 4.4.3"}, {"id": "60fdb1a5-3ac7-359a-83f0-0a230060f6d3", "product": {"name": "Cisco ThousandEyes Enterprise Agent", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "Agent 5.1"}, {"id": "b